# Files that are executed on Linux must keep LF endings regardless of the
# committer's platform. This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true)
# and deployed to Ubuntu containers/VPS — a CRLF shell script fails there with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a CRLF Dockerfile RUN line breaks builds.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
